ktura E-kolej Self-service collection Tenders and supplies Fuel wholesale prices REMIT Contact Strategy 2035 Read more E-Faktura Read more Sustainability We are implementing an energy transformation in Central Europe. We are developing in accordance with the principles of sustainable development, reducing our impact on the climate and the environment. Find out more Find out more Energy Transition ORLEN Transition Plan Decarbonisation strategy Transition projects Renewable energy sources Natural gas SMR Power grid modernisation plan Hydrogen CCUS Sustainable mobility Circular economy Sustainability Strategy GHG emissions Climate Governance Reports and policies Policies Reports Archive Local community relations officer Green finance ORLEN Group Climate Policy Read more Strategy 2035 Read more Investor relations Discover ORLEN’s dynamic business model and financial performance. Explore reports and presentations that demonstrate how we are delivering on our Strategy. Find out more Find out more Investors Dividend Shareholders structure Analyst coverage Consensus ORLEN 2035 Strategy Debt Credit rating General Meeting Corporate governance Financial calendar Reports Regulatory announcements Financial results PGNiG archive reports LOTOS archive reports Presentations Strategy 2035 Company Overview Financial presentations ORLEN in figures Macro data Teleconferences Videoconferences Financial data ORLEN w Portfelu Program IR Contacts Upstream assets spin-off Strategy 2035 Read more Dividend Read more Career Powering the future. Our development starts with you. Find out more Find out more Why ORLEN Get to know us Development Specialisations and areas of employment Benefits Internships Recruitment rules Contact Get to know us Read more Development Read more ORLEN Group Contact Polski English ORLEN Group ORLEN Administracja ORLEN Asfalt ORLEN Austria ORLEN Aviation ORLEN Baltics Retail ORLEN Biometan ORLEN Budonaft ORLEN Capital ORLEN Centrum Serwisowe ORLEN CUK ORLEN Deutschland ORLEN Eko ORLEN Kolej ORLEN Laboratorium ORLEN Lietuva ORLEN Neptun ORLEN Ochrona ORLEN OIL ORLEN Paliwa ORLEN Petrobaltic ORLEN Południe ORLEN Projekt ORLEN Projekt Ceska Republika ORLEN Serwis ORLEN Trading GmbH ORLEN Transport ORLEN Unipetrol ORLEN Upstream Polska ORLEN Upstream Canada ORLEN VC ANWIL Baltic Power Centrum Edukacji Fundacja ANWIL Fundacja ORLEN Fundacja ORLEN dla Pomorza Grupa Energa IKS Solino myORLEN Polska Press PPPT Re58 Świnoujście Offshore Terminal Technical Ship Management Usługi Logistyczne Shortcuts Fuel wholesale prices Find fuel station Products Tenders and supplies No relevant results message Number of results 0 See more Homepage Privacy policy About the company</p>\\r\\n\"}}\" id=\"text-615dec2039\" class=\"cmp-text\"> About the company Privacy policy Privacy policy Privacy Policy and Use of Cookies on the orlen.pl Website (hereinafter referred to as the \"Website\") The administrator and owner of the website www.orlen.pl is ORLEN S.A., headquartered in Płock, ul. Chemików 7, 09-411 Płock, registered in the Register of Entrepreneurs of the National Court Register maintained by the District Court for Łódź-Śródmieście in Łódź, 20th Commercial Division of the National Court Register under KRS number 0000028860, NIP 774-00-01-454, share capital/paid-in capital: PLN 1,451,177,561.25, email address: <a href=\\\"mailto:media@orlen.pl\\\">media@orlen.pl</a> (hereinafter referred to as \"ORLEN\").</p>\\r\\n<p>The Website provides information about current events and projects carried out by the ORLEN Group, press releases, photo and video materials, descriptions of our products and services, reports, employment opportunities, and the latest news and offers.</p>\\r\\n<p>This privacy policy contains information about the processing of personal data that you may provide while using the Website, as well as the use of cookies. Our goal is to protect your personal data online. We make every effort to safeguard your privacy while using the Website. We adhere to recognized international security standards, and our information security management system is independently certified and complies with ISO/IEC 27001. We have implemented framework policies, procedures, and training covering data protection, confidentiality, and security, and we regularly review the adequacy of these measures.</p>\\r\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\r\\n\"}}\" id=\"text-b8307ce8f6\" class=\"cmp-text\"> The administrator and owner of the website www.orlen.pl is ORLEN S.A., headquartered in Płock, ul. Chemików 7, 09-411 Płock, registered in the Register of Entrepreneurs of the National Court Register maintained by the District Court for Łódź-Śródmieście in Łódź, 20th Commercial Division of the National Court Register under KRS number 0000028860, NIP 774-00-01-454, share capital/paid-in capital: PLN 1,451,177,561.25, email address: media@orlen.pl (hereinafter referred to as \"ORLEN\"). The Website provides information about current events and projects carried out by the ORLEN Group, press releases, photo and video materials, descriptions of our products and services, reports, employment opportunities, and the latest news and offers. This privacy policy contains information about the processing of personal data that you may provide while using the Website, as well as the use of cookies. Our goal is to protect your personal data online. We make every effort to safeguard your privacy while using the Website. We adhere to recognized international security standards, and our information security management system is independently certified and complies with ISO/IEC 27001. We have implemented framework policies, procedures, and training covering data protection, confidentiality, and security, and we regularly review the adequacy of these measures. Cookies What are cookies used for? To ensure the proper functioning of the Website, small data files called cookies may be placed on your device. Information about the types of cookies used is provided in a banner (window), which you can access at any time&nbsp;e via <a href=\\\"#\\\" class=\\\"cookieRenew\\\">this link</a>.</p>\\r\\n<p>Some types of cookies require your consent, which you can change or withdraw at any time by setting your preferences in the banner (window) available via <a href=\\\"#\\\" class=\\\"cookieRenew\\\">this link</a>.</p>\\r\\n<p>If you consent to the use of all types of cookies, your consent will be valid for 12 months unless changed earlier. If you do not consent, your choice will be stored for 14 days.</p>\\r\\n<p>Cookies store information that the Website may need to:</p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li>adapt to how users use it,</li>\\r\\n<li>collect statistical data about the Website, e.g., which pages were visited, what elements were downloaded, and data about the domain name of the internet service provider or the country of origin of the visitor.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n\"}}\" id=\"text-9de44229a5\" class=\"cmp-text\"> To ensure the proper functioning of the Website, small data files called cookies may be placed on your device. Information about the types of cookies used is provided in a banner (window), which you can access at any time e via this link . Some types of cookies require your consent, which you can change or withdraw at any time by setting your preferences in the banner (window) available via this link . If you consent to the use of all types of cookies, your consent will be valid for 12 months unless changed earlier. If you do not consent, your choice will be stored for 14 days. Cookies store information that the Website may need to: adapt to how users use it, collect statistical data about the Website, e.g., which pages were visited, what elements were downloaded, and data about the domain name of the internet service provider or the country of origin of the visitor. Personal Data Protection Rules How do we process personal data on the Website? ORLEN S.A., headquartered in Płock, ul. Chemików 7, is the administrator of the personal data of Website users. Contact phone numbers for ORLEN S.A.: (24) 256 00 00, (24) 365 00 00, (22) 778 00 00.</p>\\r\\n\"}}\" id=\"text-9bbdb80e51\" class=\"cmp-text\"> ORLEN S.A., headquartered in Płock, ul. Chemików 7, is the administrator of the personal data of Website users. Contact phone numbers for ORLEN S.A.: (24) 256 00 00, (24) 365 00 00, (22) 778 00 00. Data Protection Officer ORLEN S.A. has appointed a Data Protection Officer who can be contacted regarding all matters related to the processing of personal data and the exercise of rights related to data processing. Detailed contact information for the Data Protection Officer is available on www.orlen.pl under the \"Contacts\" tab. To contact the Data Protection Officer, please use the following details:</p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li>address: address of the registered office of ORLEN with additional information “Inspektor Ochrony Danych” (Data Protection Officer)</li>\\r\\n<li>e-mail address: <a href=\\\"mailto:daneosobowe@orlen.pl\\\">daneosobowe@orlen.pl</a></li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n\"}}\" id=\"text-51045fa528\" class=\"cmp-text\"> ORLEN S.A. has appointed a Data Protection Officer who can be contacted regarding all matters related to the processing of personal data and the exercise of rights related to data processing. Detailed contact information for the Data Protection Officer is available on www.orlen.pl under the \"Contacts\" tab. To contact the Data Protection Officer, please use the following details: address: address of the registered office of ORLEN with additional information “Inspektor Ochrony Danych” (Data Protection Officer) e-mail address: daneosobowe@orlen.pl What are your personal data processed for? Your data will be processed to provide ORLEN S.A. services. They may also be processed to adapt the Website to usage patterns, for statistical measurements, service improvement, responding to inquiries, and detecting abuse. Additionally, with your consent, your data may be processed to send requested information from the Website.</p>\\r\\n\"}}\" id=\"text-3c55fed710\" class=\"cmp-text\"> Your data will be processed to provide ORLEN S.A. services. They may also be processed to adapt the Website to usage patterns, for statistical measurements, service improvement, responding to inquiries, and detecting abuse. Additionally, with your consent, your data may be processed to send requested information from the Website. How long will your personal data be stored? For ORLEN S.A. services, your data will be processed for the duration of service provision and, in some cases, after its completion, but only if permitted or required by law (e.g., for statistical, accounting, or claims purposes). In such cases, data will be processed for the necessary period or until you object or stop using the Website.</p>\\r\\n<p>For data processed based on your consent (e.g., sending requested information), it will be processed until the consent is withdrawn.</p>\\r\\n\"}}\" id=\"text-fe952664e9\" class=\"cmp-text\"> For ORLEN S.A. services, your data will be processed for the duration of service provision and, in some cases, after its completion, but only if permitted or required by law (e.g., for statistical, accounting, or claims purposes). In such cases, data will be processed for the necessary period or until you object or stop using the Website. For data processed based on your consent (e.g., sending requested information), it will be processed until the consent is withdrawn. Legal basis for processing your personal data For ORLEN services via the Website, your data will be processed under Article 6(1)(b) of the GDPR (necessary for the performance of a contract).</p>\\r\\n<p>For adapting the Website, marketing ORLEN’s products/services, statistical measurements, service improvement, and responding to inquiries, data will be processed under Article 6(1)(f) of the GDPR (legitimate interest of ORLEN). This includes tailoring content, ensuring service security, and continuous improvement.</p>\\r\\n<p>For sending requested information, the basis is Article 6(1)(a) of the GDPR (consent).</p>\\r\\n\"}}\" id=\"text-74698ded43\" class=\"cmp-text\"> For ORLEN services via the Website, your data will be processed under Article 6(1)(b) of the GDPR (necessary for the performance of a contract). For adapting the Website, marketing ORLEN’s products/services, statistical measurements, service improvement, and responding to inquiries, data will be processed under Article 6(1)(f) of the GDPR (legitimate interest of ORLEN). This includes tailoring content, ensuring service security, and continuous improvement. For sending requested information, the basis is Article 6(1)(a) of the GDPR (consent). Requirement to provide data Providing data is necessary to receive ORLEN services. Without it, services cannot be provided.</p>\\r\\n<p>Processing for other purposes (e.g., content personalization, statistical measurements, service improvement) is essential for high-quality service. Failure to provide data may hinder proper service delivery.</p>\\r\\n\"}}\" id=\"text-3891bbc4d7\" class=\"cmp-text\"> Providing data is necessary to receive ORLEN services. Without it, services cannot be provided. Processing for other purposes (e.g., content personalization, statistical measurements, service improvement) is essential for high-quality service. Failure to provide data may hinder proper service delivery. Who will receive your personal data? Your data may be shared with entities processing data on behalf of the administrator, such as IT service providers or marketing agencies, based on contracts and under administrator instructions.</p>\\r\\n\"}}\" id=\"text-db653a71a3\" class=\"cmp-text\"> Your data may be shared with entities processing data on behalf of the administrator, such as IT service providers or marketing agencies, based on contracts and under administrator instructions. Joint data controllership with Meta ORLEN S.A. and Meta Platforms Ireland Limited act as joint controllers of personal data processed via Meta Pixel. The scope of responsibility is defined in an agreement under Article 26 of the GDPR. Users may exercise their rights with either party, in accordance with Meta’s privacy policy: https://www.facebook.com/privacy/policy.</p>\\r\\n\"}}\" id=\"text-f7612cc543\" class=\"cmp-text\"> ORLEN S.A. and Meta Platforms Ireland Limited act as joint controllers of personal data processed via Meta Pixel. The scope of responsibility is defined in an agreement under Article 26 of the GDPR. Users may exercise their rights with either party, in accordance with Meta’s privacy policy: https://www.facebook.com/privacy/policy. Transfer of data outside the European Economic Area (EEA) Due to the use of third-party tools, personal data may be transferred to third countries, including the United States, which may not offer the same level of data protection as the EEA. In such cases, data transfer is based on appropriate legal safeguards, such as standard contractual clauses approved by the European Commission.</p>\\r\\n\"}}\" id=\"text-200d06376f\" class=\"cmp-text\"> Due to the use of third-party tools, personal data may be transferred to third countries, including the United States, which may not offer the same level of data protection as the EEA. In such cases, data transfer is based on appropriate legal safeguards, such as standard contractual clauses approved by the European Commission. Profiling and its impact The Website may involve profiling, i.e., automated processing of personal data to analyze or predict user preferences for marketing content customization. Profiling does not have legal effects or similarly significant impacts on users. Users have the right to object to profiling by contacting the Data Protection Officer.</p>\\r\\n\"}}\" id=\"text-2194a898db\" class=\"cmp-text\"> The Website may involve profiling, i.e., automated processing of personal data to analyze or predict user preferences for marketing content customization. Profiling does not have legal effects or similarly significant impacts on users. Users have the right to object to profiling by contacting the Data Protection Officer. What are your rights related to the processing of your personal data? You have the following rights:</p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li>Right to access your data,</li>\\r\\n<li>Right to request data rectification,</li>\\r\\n<li>Right to data deletion (in specific situations),</li>\\r\\n<li>Right to lodge a complaint with the data protection authority,</li>\\r\\n<li>Right to restrict data processing.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n<p>If your data is processed based on consent or for service provision, you also have:</p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li>Right to withdraw consent (without affecting prior lawful processing),</li>\\r\\n<li>Right to data portability (receive your data in a structured, machine-readable format and transfer it to another controller).</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n<p>To exercise these rights, contact the data administrator or Data Protection Officer using the contact details above.</p>\\r\\n<p>You also have the right to lodge a complaint with the President of the Personal Data Protection Office. Requests can be sent to: daneosobowe@orlen.pl or by mail with the note \"Data Protection Officer\".</p>\\r\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\r\\n\"}}\" id=\"text-2dbca4d04e\" class=\"cmp-text\"> You have the following rights: Right to access your data, Right to request data rectification, Right to data deletion (in specific situations), Right to lodge a complaint with the data protection authority, Right to restrict data processing. If your data is processed based on consent or for service provision, you also have: Right to withdraw consent (without affecting prior lawful processing), Right to data portability (receive your data in a structured, machine-readable format and transfer it to another controller). To exercise these rights, contact the data administrator or Data Protection Officer using the contact details above. You also have the right to lodge a complaint with the President of the Personal Data Protection Office. Requests can be sent to: daneosobowe@orlen.pl or by mail with the note \"Data Protection Officer\". Final Provisions Services and features of the Website may expand over time. ORLEN S.A. may update this document accordingly. Changes will be announced via the Website, and each new version will include a new date. Significant changes will be clearly highlighted. This document is for informational purposes.</p>\\r\\n\"}}\" id=\"text-a625d4a3da\" class=\"cmp-text\"> Services and features of the Website may expand over time. ORLEN S.A. may update this document accordingly. Changes will be announced via the Website, and each new version will include a new date. Significant changes will be clearly highlighted. This document is for informational purposes. ORLEN Copyright © 1996-2025 All rights reserved Shortcuts For business Tenders and supplies Fuel stations VITAY Program About the company Our vision Press-pack Report a question or complaint Sitemap Privacy policy Legal disclaimer Personal data" 1 :add]
